  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. All 8 original items and 3 of the 4 that arrived while I worked are closed. One is left open on purpose.\n\nOriginal items:\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT urogram: no cause found for the hematuria; incidental 4 mm left lower lobe nodule. I first ordered a CT chest in about 12 months (sr-t0001) and messaged him. A Lakeshore fax that arrived later changed this plan (below).\n- pt-0016: TSH normal. Potassium was corrected from 6.3 to 4.4 (analyzer error). Both closed with no action.\n- pt-0007 Leslie Parisian, preliminary CTA chest: the final report (dr-00084) says no PE and no nodule (the \"nodule\" was a vessel) and needs no follow-up. Closed.\n- pt-0007, BMP: creatinine 0.98 → 1.64 within 35 h meets the kidney injury rule. Urgent repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0009, by 10/26), urgent message sent, note written. He has naproxen as needed on his list; I flagged it for you to consider stopping and left it unchanged.\n- pt-0065, Lakeshore lung screening addendum (Lung-RADS 4A): the fax's date of birth (1951-08-04) and MRN (4471-20) don't match our Judith Nowicki (1960-03-22, MRN 0388-83), and no other patient matches. I took no action in her chart. RN triage has an urgent task (task-t0013) to tell Lakeshore today so the result reaches the right patient's clinician, and to have the fax removed from her chart. Note written.\n- pt-0033 Carol Whitfield, creatinine 1.31: not a kidney injury. The 0.84 from 10/21 is entered in error and was left out. Closed.\n- pt-0008 Walter Brennan, potassium 6.4 flagged hemolyzed: I first ordered an urgent repeat BMP and messaged him. This changed after a correction (below).\n\nArrivals and changed decisions:\n- pt-0008: the lab corrected the result. The specimen was not hemolyzed, so the 6.4 is likely real. I switched to the stat pathway: STAT BMP today (sr-t0021), on-call notified at stat priority, and a corrected message telling him to come in today. On his medication review, metoprolol is the only drug that may raise potassium. I didn't hold it because of his ischemic heart disease. Addendum note written.\n- pt-0033: a later urgent care creatinine of 1.78 (0.47 above the 1.31 nine hours earlier) does meet the kidney injury rule. Urgent repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0026, by 10/26), patient messaged, note written. I flagged hydrochlorothiazide for you to consider holding and changed nothing.\n- pt-0006: a Lakeshore addendum shows he is already in lung cancer screening. His April LDCT is now Lung-RADS 3 (new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule), with an LDCT due by 11/14. I ordered that LDCT (sr-t0030, today through 11/14), added a tracking task, sent a corrected message, and wrote an addendum note.\n\nLeft open: inbox-a0002 (pt-0007 chest X-ray). It is a preliminary report (possible 7 mm nodule) with no final version yet, so policy says to leave it open.\n\nNeeds your action in the EHR: my tools can't cancel these orders or the CT tracking task, so please cancel them:\n1. pt-0006: the CT chest order sr-t0001 and its tracking task task-t0002. The scheduling pool has a task not to schedule it (task-t0032).\n2. pt-0008: the urgent repeat BMP sr-t0017. The STAT BMP replaces it, so only one draw is needed.\n\nNot touched: six refill messages in your messages queue, all received before I started and outside the results inbox.",
